{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq7hef9ato1","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"[ingest] Self-signed certs can't shortcut local HTTPS — mkcert is required","summary":"TLS validates the cert's ISSUER against the system trust store regardless of localhost, so a self-signed cert (its own untrusted issuer) is rejected. `mkcert -install` adds a trusted local CA (the password step), which is the whole reason it works. Needed only for the custom-connector inline-MCP-UI path.","created_by":"onboard-learn","valid_from":"2026-06-10T03:00:40.510Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:01:05.747Z"}
{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mq7hef9ato1","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/cloude","title":"[ingest] Self-signed certs can't shortcut local HTTPS — mkcert is required","summary":"TLS validates the cert's ISSUER against the system trust store regardless of localhost, so a self-signed cert (its own untrusted issuer) is rejected. `mkcert -install` adds a trusted local CA (the password step), which is the whole reason it works. Needed only for the custom-connector inline-MCP-UI path.","created_by":"onboard-learn","valid_from":"2026-06-10T03:00:40.510Z","actor":"overlay-sync","ts":"2026-06-10T19:08:57.822Z"}
